/// The guest SDK's binary-state fixture: a component built on `brenn-guest`
/// whose retained state is bytes, published as `application/octet-stream`
/// through `RetainedState` and a hand-written `StateCodec`. It is driven by
/// text commands on `in` and publishes one untyped report per activation on
/// `report`: the `feed` window as the SDK reads it, and the result of every
/// command. `state` carries the binary state, and its channel or binding must
/// be declared `non_text`.
///
/// `log` is required because a state recovered under `StateLoss::Recover` is
/// logged.
component ProcessorSdkBytesTest {
  abi = processor;
  requires = [ports, log];
  in in;
  optional in feed;
  io state;
  out report;
}
